WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.961 --> 00:00:20.118
The warship continued to fire at us. Cannonballs fell into the sea around us, but none of them touched the Nautilus.

2
00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:27.293
If any of them hit the submarine, we would be in serious trouble, yet Captain Nemo did not appear on the platform.

3
00:00:27.294 --> 00:00:32.634
"Professor, we must do everything we can to get out of this situation," said Ned.

4
00:00:32.635 --> 00:00:34.777
Conseil nodded in agreement.

5
00:00:34.778 --> 00:00:42.277
"Let's try to signal the warship," said Ned. "Perhaps then they'll understand that we're good people, not connected to Captain Nemo."

6
00:00:42.278 --> 00:00:45.214
Ned pulled out his handkerchief to wave in the air.

7
00:00:45.215 --> 00:00:49.848
But he had scarcely revealed it when he was struck by a fist and fell to the deck.

8
00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:56.348
"Fool! What do you think you're doing?" bellowed Captain Nemo, whose arrival had gone unnoticed.

9
00:00:56.349 --> 00:01:02.507
The captain's face was purple with rage as he roared at Ned and shook the harpooner by the shoulders.

10
00:01:02.508 --> 00:01:10.086
Then he abandoned Ned and turned to face the warship, which was still raining cannonballs onto the sea around the Nautilus.

11
00:01:10.087 --> 00:01:16.911
"So, ship of a cursed nation, you know who I am!" said Captain Nemo in a powerful voice.

12
00:01:16.912 --> 00:01:22.252
"I don't need to see your flag to know who you are, but I'll show you mine!"

13
00:01:22.253 --> 00:01:27.578
The captain held up a black flag similar to the one he had placed at the South Pole.

14
00:01:27.579 --> 00:01:35.816
At that moment a cannonball struck the Nautilus without damaging it and bounced into the sea. The captain seemed unfazed.

15
00:01:35.817 --> 00:01:40.705
"Go below!" he said to me. "You and your companions, go below now!"

16
00:01:40.706 --> 00:01:44.887
"Captain, are you going to attack that vessel?" I asked.

17
00:01:44.888 --> 00:01:48.387
"Professor, I'm going to sink it."

18
00:01:48.388 --> 00:01:51.308
"You wouldn't do that!" I said in horror.

19
00:01:51.309 --> 00:02:01.371
"I will," he said coldly, "and I advise you not to judge me. Fate has shown you what you ought not to have seen. The attack has begun."

20
00:02:01.372 --> 00:02:05.959
"What is this vessel that attacks us? What country does it represent?"

21
00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:11.014
"It's better if you don't know. I say to you once more: Go below."

22
00:02:11.015 --> 00:02:19.609
There was nothing for us to do but obey. About fifteen crew members surrounded the captain, all looking with hatred at the approaching vessel.

23
00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:23.704
The same desire for vengeance seemed to fill every soul.

24
00:02:23.705 --> 00:02:31.627
I was leaving the platform at the moment another projectile struck the Nautilus, and I heard the captain shouting, "Strike, mad vessel!

25
00:02:31.628 --> 00:02:34.470
Shower us with your useless cannonballs.

26
00:02:34.471 --> 00:02:39.010
You'll never escape the battering ram of the Nautilus, but you won't perish here.

27
00:02:39.011 --> 00:02:43.681
I won't have your wreckage mingling with that of the sacred Avenger!"

28
00:02:43.682 --> 00:02:48.427
I returned to the gallery, where I could see by the instruments that we were speeding up.

29
00:02:48.428 --> 00:02:52.340
The Nautilus was soon beyond range of the warship's guns.

30
00:02:52.341 --> 00:02:55.903
Around four in the afternoon, I returned to the platform.

31
00:02:55.904 --> 00:03:00.657
The captain was pacing while looking at the ship, now five or six miles away.

32
00:03:00.658 --> 00:03:04.570
He allowed it to pursue us, but he did not attack.

33
00:03:04.571 --> 00:03:10.157
Perhaps if I said something, I could put a stop to this terrible episode before it began.

34
00:03:10.158 --> 00:03:12.165
"Captain—" I said.

35
00:03:12.166 --> 00:03:22.485
"Silence!" he roared. "I am the law and I am the judge! I am the oppressed and on that ship is the oppressor!

36
00:03:22.486 --> 00:03:32.088
Thanks to him, I have lost all that I loved, cherished, and respected—country, wife, children, father, and mother.

37
00:03:32.089 --> 00:03:41.715
I saw all of them perish! All that I hate is there! I have nothing to discuss with you, Professor Aronnax."

38
00:03:41.716 --> 00:03:49.294
I cast a last look at the warship, which was steaming toward us, and joined Ned and Conseil in the gallery.

39
00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:56.546
"We must flee this submarine!" I exclaimed. "I don't know where that warship is from, but it will be sunk before night.

40
00:03:56.547 --> 00:04:03.041
In any case, it's better for us to perish with it than to be part of a revenge that we don't fully understand."

41
00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:11.112
"I agree," said Ned. "The moon should be almost full tonight. We can escape when the ship is near enough to hear us or see us."

42
00:04:11.113 --> 00:04:14.691
Night arrived and the Nautilus remained on the surface.

43
00:04:14.692 --> 00:04:18.858
Several times I thought the submarine was preparing to attack.

44
00:04:18.859 --> 00:04:24.509
But instead Captain Nemo continued to allow his enemy to approach before darting ahead of it.

45
00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:28.421
The three of us waited for our opportunity to take action.

46
00:04:28.422 --> 00:04:36.834
We hardly spoke at all because we were too nervous. Several times Ned wanted to throw himself into the water, but I forced him to wait.

47
00:04:36.835 --> 00:04:42.160
At three o'clock in the morning, full of uneasiness, I mounted the platform.

48
00:04:42.161 --> 00:04:46.676
Captain Nemo was standing near his flag, which was blowing in the wind.

49
00:04:46.677 --> 00:04:55.835
His eyes never left the warship. The intensity of his look seemed to draw it toward us more surely than if we had been towing it.

50
00:04:55.836 --> 00:04:59.977
The moon was overhead, and Jupiter was rising in the east.

51
00:04:59.978 --> 00:05:06.723
The sky and the sea rivaled each other in tranquility while passions boiled aboard the Nautilus.

52
00:05:06.724 --> 00:05:11.906
I remained on the platform until six o'clock without Captain Nemo speaking to me.

53
00:05:11.907 --> 00:05:18.390
The warship lay about a mile and a half from us, and it began firing again with the first light of day.

54
00:05:18.391 --> 00:05:25.223
The moment was approaching when the Nautilus would attack its enemy, and my companions and I would leave Captain Nemo forever.

55
00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:32.390
The lieutenant came up on the platform, accompanied by several crewmen, who began to prepare for battle.

56
00:05:32.391 --> 00:05:40.382
The railing around the platform was removed; the pilothouse and electric light were lowered until they were level with the surface of the submarine.

57
00:05:40.383 --> 00:05:43.086
I returned to my companions in the gallery.

58
00:05:43.087 --> 00:05:49.096
The Nautilus was slowing down, and I knew that Captain Nemo was allowing the warship to draw near.

59
00:05:49.097 --> 00:05:52.953
Now I could hear the sound of cannon fire more distinctly.

60
00:05:52.954 --> 00:05:57.430
"My friends, the hour for battle has arrived," I announced.

61
00:05:57.431 --> 00:06:04.160
Ned was determined, Conseil calm, myself so nervous that I didn't know what to do.

62
00:06:04.161 --> 00:06:12.923
We went into the library; from here all we had to do was pass through a door, climb the stairs to the platform, and make our escape.

63
00:06:12.924 --> 00:06:17.422
But the moment I opened the door, I heard the hatch above us slam shut.

64
00:06:17.423 --> 00:06:20.589
As Ned rushed onto the stairs, I stopped him.

65
00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:26.573
A familiar hissing told me that the reservoirs were filling and the submarine was descending.

66
00:06:26.574 --> 00:06:29.057
I understood the maneuver.

67
00:06:29.058 --> 00:06:36.740
Captain Nemo wanted to strike the warship from underwater, where the bottom of the ship lacked protective plating and was most vulnerable.

68
00:06:36.741 --> 00:06:40.835
We scarcely had time to think, but took refuge in my cabin.

69
00:06:40.836 --> 00:06:46.660
I waited and listened intently; all my senses concentrated in my hearing.

70
00:06:46.661 --> 00:06:52.716
The Nautilus accelerated, and I knew it was preparing to attack the ship with the battering ram on its bow.

71
00:06:52.717 --> 00:06:57.573
The whole submarine trembled as it hit the warship. I screamed!

72
00:06:57.574 --> 00:07:05.986
Unable to stand it any longer, I ran to the gallery. Captain Nemo was standing before one of the windows, watching the warship sink.

73
00:07:05.987 --> 00:07:11.645
I could not bear to look. When it was all over, he returned to his cabin.

74
00:07:11.646 --> 00:07:18.468
Through the open door, I saw a portrait of a young woman, undoubtedly his wife, and his two children.

75
00:07:18.469 --> 00:07:26.667
Captain Nemo gazed at them, stretched out his arms, and kneeling down, burst into sobs.
